Subject: [PATCH 07240/11362] [outer-loop] bp35 L9 round 25 (gpt-5.6-sol, max
 effort): retracts round 23's universal viewport-survival law with 2
 independently-verified counter-examples

Dispatched gpt-5.6-sol at MAX reasoning effort (vs round 24's default xhigh)
with a fresh brief pointing beyond round 24's exhausted candidate list.
Result: a genuine, significant correction to standing project knowledge.

Round 23 established: a flight survives iff its landing rest lies within
the camera view active when the flight starts (derived from 2 observed
ascent deaths). Round 25 found 3 counter-examples where the player survives
crossing/landing outside the starting viewport via camera pan-and-reacquire:
a 48-row unsupported DOWN fall, a 48-row UP flight landing 19.5 rows above
the starting top, and an UP flight to a previously-unvisited destination.
The retraction is correctly scoped -- it does NOT claim the known
ungrown-gap-float and door-column ascent deaths are now safe (those were
not re-tested and remain real per bounded_negative_results); it narrows the
open question to "why do some offscreen landings pan/reacquire while others
still kill."

Also found: ACTION7 is a full-state rewind for flights and switches (not a
mid-animation abort -- it jumps between complete settled states only); a new
3-action sparse descent route (13 actions shorter than the prior 16-action
path); the one untested reachable-switch order and a fresh 84-frame glyph
census were both null.

Given the magnitude of this claim (retracting previously-verified project
mechanics), independently re-verified before committing rather than
trusting the report: reviewed the full artifact structure, ran
scripts/adversarial_verify.py myself (0 flagged), and -- most importantly --
independently re-derived BOTH load-bearing counter-examples from scratch
using separate frame-registration code I wrote earlier this session. Both
matched the artifact's own numbers closely (DOWN fall: camera pan starting
~layer 25, final camera +22, player world row 50.5, alive; UP flight: pan
starting layer 24, final camera -36, player world row 2.5, alive) and
confirmed the raw alive/GAME_OVER ground truth 3x from fresh environments
for all three claimed-safe sequences. Also spawned an independent hostile-
reviewer sub-agent (its one finding was the same solve_provenance false
positive already resolved for round 24 -- adapter-free public-frame
exploration is correctly tagged live_agent_self_discovery per CLAUDE.md's
taxonomy, verified against the taxonomy text directly).

No new rest above -9.5, no new level, frontier unchanged at 8/9.

Evidence: results/outer_loop_round25_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json

